<p>Frank L. Nigey built three-story brick hotel in 1906 targeting the "luxury" market then served only by the InterOcean Hotel located one block closer to the Northern Pacific Railway depot. Built in electrical utilities and hot and cold running water piped to all rooms. Common bathrooms provided on every floor. Local and long distance telephone service available on-site.</p>

